==== a version literal is a reference with a string index
version "1.2.3"
----
(ref "version" (str "1.2.3"))

==== a one-component version literal is the same shape
version "14"
----
(ref "version" (str "14"))

==== a string cast to version is a cast, not a reference
"1.2.3" as version
----
(cast (str "1.2.3") "version")

==== version as a property of an object is an of chain
version of operating system
----
(of (ref "version") (ref "operating system"))

==== pad of wraps the version literal, not the comparison
pad of version "1.2"
----
(of (ref "pad") (ref "version" (str "1.2")))

==== a padded comparison keeps pad on each side
pad of version "1.2" > pad of version "1.2.3"
----
(bin ">" (of (ref "pad") (ref "version" (str "1.2")))
         (of (ref "pad") (ref "version" (str "1.2.3"))))

==== a version literal compared against a bare string
version "2.10.1" > "2.3.3"
----
(bin ">" (ref "version" (str "2.10.1")) (str "2.3.3"))

==== a cast binds tighter than the comparison it sits in
"2.10.1" > "2.3.3" as version
----
(bin ">" (str "2.10.1") (cast (str "2.3.3") "version"))

==== the operator spelling is kept as written, not canonicalized
version of operating system >= version "14"
----
(bin ">=" (of (ref "version") (ref "operating system")) (ref "version" (str "14")))

==== strverscmp version is a distinct multi-word cast target
"1.2.3" as strverscmp version
----
(cast (str "1.2.3") "strverscmp version")
